---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { datasetStats, fixesForDefect } from '../lib/data';
import { SITE } from '../site';

const defects = (await getCollection('defects')).sort(
  (a, b) => a.data.commonness - b.data.commonness,
);
const topDefects = defects.slice(0, 6);
const stats = datasetStats();
---

<Base title={SITE.name} description={SITE.description}>
  <div class="canvas">

    <!-- ── Opening ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="spread">
      <div class="stack-md">
        <p class="eyebrow">3D printing · settings &amp; failure database</p>
        <h1 class="title">Your print failed. The answer depends on your printer and your filament — so the answer should ask.</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          Search a defect and you get a blog post written for someone else's
          machine. {SITE.name} keeps the settings as structured data, filters it
          to what you are actually running, and shows the reasoning and the
          evidence behind every recommendation.
        </p>
        <p><a class="cta" href="/fix/">Diagnose a failed print →</a></p>
      </div>

      <aside class="rail">
        <div class="note">
          <span class="note__label">In the database</span>
          <dl>
            <dt>Defects</dt><dd>{defects.length}</dd>
            <dt>Fixes</dt><dd>{stats.fixes}</dd>
            <dt>Materials</dt><dd>{stats.materials}</dd>
            <dt>Printer classes</dt><dd>{stats.printerClasses}</dd>
            <dt>Verified</dt><dd>{stats.verified}</dd>
          </dl>
        </div>
        <div class="note note--caveat">
          <span class="note__label">Read the last row</span>
          Verified results are submitted outcomes, and there are none yet. The
          fixes come from manufacturer guidance and established practice. When
          that number starts moving it will mean something, which is exactly why
          it is not being rounded up today.
        </div>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <div class="tick-rule" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>

    <!-- ── Common defects ───────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="spread">
      <div>
        <h2 class="section-heading">Start with what you can see</h2>
        <p class="lead" style="margin-top: var(--space-3);">
          The six failures that account for most ruined prints.
        </p>

        <ul class="defect-grid">
          {topDefects.map((defect) => (
            <li>
              <a href={`/defects/${defect.id}/`}>
                <span class="defect-grid__title">{defect.data.title}</span>
                <span class="defect-grid__count">{fixesForDefect(defect.id).length} fixes</span>
              </a>
              <p class="defect-grid__summary">{defect.data.summary}</p>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>

        <p style="margin-top: var(--space-6);"><a href="/defects/">All {defects.length} defects →</a></p>
      </div>

      <aside class="rail">
        <div class="note">
          <span class="note__label">Not sure what you are looking at?</span>
          Several defects look alike — warping and adhesion failure get confused
          constantly. Every page has a table for telling them apart.
        </div>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <div class="tick-rule" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>

    <!-- ── Why this is different ────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="spread">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2 class="section-heading">Why the advice elsewhere keeps not working</h2>
        <p>
          Almost all printing advice is written without knowing what you own. A
          retraction figure that fixes stringing on a Bowden machine will cause
          grinding and heat creep on a direct-drive one. Turning the fan up
          rescues an overhang and ruins layer bonding in ABS. The advice is not
          wrong — it is answering a question about a different printer.
        </p>
        <p>
          So the settings here are stored as data with the conditions attached,
          and filtered before you see them. Fixes that do not apply to your setup
          are removed rather than listed with a caveat you will skim past.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every fix also carries how confident we are and how many real results
          support it. Today most of those counts are zero. Publishing them as
          zero is the whole point — a number nobody can check is not evidence,
          and a dataset that starts by inflating itself is worthless the first
          time anyone tests it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="rail">
        <div class="note">
          <span class="note__label">How it is funded</span>
          The database and the diagnostic are free. A paid tier for people who
          sell prints is what pays for the work. No vendor pays for placement.
        </div>
        <div class="note">
          <span class="note__label">Published by</span>
          {SITE.operator.name} ({SITE.operator.legalName}), {SITE.operator.country}.
        </div>
      </aside>
    </section>

  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .cta {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font-data);
    font-size: var(--size-s);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wide);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-5);
    border: var(--border-hair) solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: background-color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease),
                color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease);
  }
  .cta:hover { background: var(--accent); color: var(--paper); }

  .defect-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(15rem, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-5);
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .defect-grid > li {
    padding-top: var(--space-4);
    border-top: var(--rule-accent-width) solid var(--rule);
  }
  .defect-grid a {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .defect-grid a:hover .defect-grid__title { color: var(--accent); }
  .defect-grid__title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--size-l);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-tight);
  }
  .defect-grid__count {
    flex: none;
    font-family: var(--font-data);
    font-size: var(--size-3xs);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wide);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
  }
  .defect-grid__summary {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
    font-size: var(--size-s);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }
</style>
